WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.792
Recursive queries require extra care.

00:00:02.792 --> 00:00:06.197
A wrong join condition can produce too many rows.

00:00:06.197 --> 00:00:10.947
Cycles in the source hierarchy can also create problematic traversal.

00:00:10.947 --> 00:00:13.062
Test the anchor by itself.

00:00:13.062 --> 00:00:18.957
Inspect the recursive join. Use depth or path information while developing the query.

00:00:18.957 --> 00:00:22.842
Start with a small dataset so the behavior is visible.

00:00:22.842 --> 00:00:29.907
Recursive CTEs are useful when rows refer to other rows in a hierarchy or graph-like chain.

00:00:29.907 --> 00:00:35.472
The anchor establishes the starting set; the recursive term finds the next level.

00:00:35.472 --> 00:00:38.517
Always think about termination and cycles.

00:00:38.517 --> 00:00:43.189
Production hierarchies often need safeguards against malformed relationships.
